[{:db/id "q-159658/selection/c851c370be44a541ec1b52b5efb038e934d737e9c25ebdf3d03cc9561c3ba41a" :answer/id #uuid "39662ffe-3427-5f74-b509-385d247ec294" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159658/selection/090879b1a16d3a4d75d998f06b2066dd3cfc46b6541cc7b173b1dbaeb47c8c58" :answer/id #uuid "c5158365-736d-563f-9720-a896581a716d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2x\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159658/selection/a80ee7f0850b07455c13a572f0dcc717e55d81d5e013e9fd08c49879978705dd" :answer/id #uuid "d1877610-3f44-5502-9c47-bb4b9838754c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159658/selection/bebee34b6723bb8c3a1476b82387fdcf2abf1db1aed20aaa679d601307ea3f04" :answer/id #uuid "3e5aac6c-fdcb-58d5-af3b-3cda85568fff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159658/selection/5d4712af9fadfb80f0a3c43433e02cd9802f8f485af1f2a022e610c110fc404a" :answer/id #uuid "d75894c6-0b46-526c-beea-084d2b197067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159658/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1c2334f-bd50-569a-bb66-6ebffa35318c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159658/selection/a80ee7f0850b07455c13a572f0dcc717e55d81d5e013e9fd08c49879978705dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-159658/selection/c851c370be44a541ec1b52b5efb038e934d737e9c25ebdf3d03cc9561c3ba41a" "q-159658/selection/090879b1a16d3a4d75d998f06b2066dd3cfc46b6541cc7b173b1dbaeb47c8c58" "q-159658/selection/a80ee7f0850b07455c13a572f0dcc717e55d81d5e013e9fd08c49879978705dd" "q-159658/selection/bebee34b6723bb8c3a1476b82387fdcf2abf1db1aed20aaa679d601307ea3f04" "q-159658/selection/5d4712af9fadfb80f0a3c43433e02cd9802f8f485af1f2a022e610c110fc404a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159658" :question/id #uuid "84882c75-fbb0-5e5f-ad0e-928900017882" :question/math-academy-id "q-159658" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2xy-1}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and the constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}(2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot (2x\\cdot 1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159658/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35718"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}y,$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y) & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+{x}^{2}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x{e}^{xy}\\cdot (1)+{x}^{2} \\\\  & =x{e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660/selection/150f9030943d4d08e783f7c5f4221116c053a3a2a5f9bc3efc6d3979d50d41ef" :answer/id #uuid "488422f0-c3e5-5c7e-868f-203325676aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660/selection/9ac8d8f6c1ef0aa7fe7d500c405269968b04d8c0d99f17def485f7a76db6d051" :answer/id #uuid "68107968-0b55-53bf-a708-735e997826be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660/selection/c2504524716cd00ef228b78ddcf6ef09c2e45cec8ef42f3c273b642ac24f94dd" :answer/id #uuid "2f6ea151-d148-579e-98e9-8a5857ca2c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "f3ee3f0e-e153-5075-82e1-f6a246bdc922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660/selection/30d771277e5f88c2a08a4e446b7ea080dd38abbdbbc820f6d698c4b2c0bc77a1" :answer/id #uuid "570e2a01-6a95-527e-9b80-c01e84878a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd36a4f6-1d5e-54ce-be34-89b01ecdb987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159660/selection/9ac8d8f6c1ef0aa7fe7d500c405269968b04d8c0d99f17def485f7a76db6d051" :answer-field/choices ["q-159660/selection/150f9030943d4d08e783f7c5f4221116c053a3a2a5f9bc3efc6d3979d50d41ef" "q-159660/selection/9ac8d8f6c1ef0aa7fe7d500c405269968b04d8c0d99f17def485f7a76db6d051" "q-159660/selection/c2504524716cd00ef228b78ddcf6ef09c2e45cec8ef42f3c273b642ac24f94dd" "q-159660/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" "q-159660/selection/30d771277e5f88c2a08a4e446b7ea080dd38abbdbbc820f6d698c4b2c0bc77a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159660" :question/id #uuid "2cf8e1bf-4d61-5043-9e78-9d1d07ae32ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-159660" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159660/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713/selection/577f1a9798ec435c864e1dba413a38db21e0e9ee8ca50c800025311bde62780e" :answer/id #uuid "10a90859-36d7-5724-99d7-c7a175c77722" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713/selection/af0b8b71f30c12ce1de7ed963c33cc313ce8e4580fc2735fcb6b93ea953354d8" :answer/id #uuid "f3b07d9c-0271-5c5e-9ba5-7447f26e22b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713/selection/e12be3376d9550af044fadc38c551ce202a9db35097dda89e9d598bc28de188f" :answer/id #uuid "cab8a909-340a-5940-8d09-02fc459e24a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713/selection/9526d92ff1e64a388b8af9b22f25f261a890a0435738983d507c1c404fd4d05d" :answer/id #uuid "4967a27b-dcfa-5635-877f-57347de9a89d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y(x+1)^{2y-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713/selection/f8f561f8b47b91491ca10bf3ffeca0609b9404159e66938fd6186409b5002bb7" :answer/id #uuid "d7c04959-279e-589e-8fe6-d8416de9f250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "45fed4a4-b3ae-5a1b-a914-62c399e435a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35713/selection/577f1a9798ec435c864e1dba413a38db21e0e9ee8ca50c800025311bde62780e" :answer-field/choices ["q-35713/selection/577f1a9798ec435c864e1dba413a38db21e0e9ee8ca50c800025311bde62780e" "q-35713/selection/af0b8b71f30c12ce1de7ed963c33cc313ce8e4580fc2735fcb6b93ea953354d8" "q-35713/selection/e12be3376d9550af044fadc38c551ce202a9db35097dda89e9d598bc28de188f" "q-35713/selection/9526d92ff1e64a388b8af9b22f25f261a890a0435738983d507c1c404fd4d05d" "q-35713/selection/f8f561f8b47b91491ca10bf3ffeca0609b9404159e66938fd6186409b5002bb7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35713" :question/id #uuid "bcac2fd7-4ed3-57e6-9593-aacaa7508a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-35713" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+1)^{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1) & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (1+0) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35713/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35713"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656/selection/f2a7e74b19ae540806afc509df0e2d80b55a49374bce18968b4017dcb639b628" :answer/id #uuid "ceb29826-414c-58bc-af2e-da23d2cb0e96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656/selection/8355ef143082e099ba9784797436895763f93e66427f35eccab4503031d947b1" :answer/id #uuid "23b0bbd3-2469-5dba-b867-9982d62ddcbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656/selection/67f7d4901544df82435335e4fe9194b70586a0372f9727b96abffe4af68f92ba" :answer/id #uuid "11caa765-db5e-562d-8949-2d15235e8758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656/selection/7ed11e3e6ac8b15f66c2098a84532bfdde87f24d18f5ec746b2cc74a0c451ed1" :answer/id #uuid "b8d05e49-de30-5a20-9b84-75fa8d64a8f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656/selection/321744f55ebed0a28b73a3f10fce8293051897475350c017647cd1449535e70f" :answer/id #uuid "5e287542-a75c-5c22-bbb5-c406a76e87b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a355a4ea-1b10-5d8e-a146-28a6f0966803" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159656/selection/67f7d4901544df82435335e4fe9194b70586a0372f9727b96abffe4af68f92ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-159656/selection/f2a7e74b19ae540806afc509df0e2d80b55a49374bce18968b4017dcb639b628" "q-159656/selection/8355ef143082e099ba9784797436895763f93e66427f35eccab4503031d947b1" "q-159656/selection/67f7d4901544df82435335e4fe9194b70586a0372f9727b96abffe4af68f92ba" "q-159656/selection/7ed11e3e6ac8b15f66c2098a84532bfdde87f24d18f5ec746b2cc74a0c451ed1" "q-159656/selection/321744f55ebed0a28b73a3f10fce8293051897475350c017647cd1449535e70f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159656" :question/id #uuid "f5b2ae4a-57b2-54a4-b907-816f60555712" :question/math-academy-id "q-159656" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot 2x-y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "afe3e5cf-2b48-5630-9e1b-e16dbe2b475a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768/selection/b5be7d38503dcbf1896dc73e5bd6ccf72db0ba1c926b6910aad76337483f2ff5" :answer/id #uuid "94a3c8a4-8b8a-5daa-9abe-1a69a4a1d7c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768/selection/b26995010ab06fdf5eabbb1a8db8813898f1a25389264c5639bbb75ce37d1ddd" :answer/id #uuid "8cef5789-eced-5f56-b32e-efb38dc3e40f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "45b8d6cb-eafa-56d9-a0ed-1ad007dead4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768/selection/7e1191cb03644646f9e975eff25bd01f693a7176c7d0081cf70750a65f5909da" :answer/id #uuid "30dbb420-483f-5d1f-a7d3-a2f4b602a962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a03980-1c6a-5c4e-9bd4-6bbd7ae57d71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159768/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-159768/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-159768/selection/b5be7d38503dcbf1896dc73e5bd6ccf72db0ba1c926b6910aad76337483f2ff5" "q-159768/selection/b26995010ab06fdf5eabbb1a8db8813898f1a25389264c5639bbb75ce37d1ddd" "q-159768/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-159768/selection/7e1191cb03644646f9e975eff25bd01f693a7176c7d0081cf70750a65f5909da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159768" :question/id #uuid "8f954155-7c22-5e6e-a4d1-3429c98b0a35" :question/math-academy-id "q-159768" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & =x(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi )} & =2\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =2(-1-\\pi \\cdot 0)+(-1) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159768/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159768"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "b73e783a-b5f2-5297-b4fe-4124eccb1bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "263c67a4-1b69-51b0-8e49-99f1b62d6596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer/id #uuid "2b013f7d-6b9d-52fa-a67d-131252d6bde1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "80e995c1-7f73-5e90-81d9-ee1596f15b62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "e5087c73-7cfe-5e82-b3d7-bcc2bd0d9d9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec92e6d8-b395-5680-8f28-95e0b23dd36f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159766/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer-field/choices ["q-159766/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-159766/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-159766/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" "q-159766/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" "q-159766/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159766" :question/id #uuid "834163bd-4e3f-5a32-83f7-f9500712f022" :question/math-academy-id "q-159766" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(2,\\sqrt{5}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain, the sum, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) & =1\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot 0+2y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\sqrt{5})} & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}+\\frac{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+5}+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{4+5}} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159766/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159766"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-159751"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot {e}^{xy}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}))-{x}^{2}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot {e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy))-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =({e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y))-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =({e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot 1)-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}-2{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & ={e}^{1\\cdot 1}+1\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 1}-2\\cdot {1}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =e+e-2 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "3086d83d-61bb-59e7-b185-643aeb330f80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "14af26d2-5137-5aa6-bd3e-5e0137f114d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8a9b0047-327d-524d-a74c-ee9e3db6880a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9c12fa1d-6b4e-5d2f-ad17-20619c9aef19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "94095686-fb03-5489-8d44-ed74c6110c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f81703f5-6968-5d08-83d1-262086ef4abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159752/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-159752/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-159752/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-159752/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-159752/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-159752/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159752" :question/id #uuid "b3aac067-ce23-515b-b5c8-0d28c68fc2b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-159752" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1+\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1/4,4)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4)+1+\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159752/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159752"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716/selection/269a36d49266519ed5dab217c7664817e5da284d03c67290a620939af15a036d" :answer/id #uuid "e9728124-f97b-5a9b-acad-a73f18baaba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716/selection/13a2f7f94d95f46bf33f1c60a64505c798a5d8b7e91b2da1ffb8193348014d98" :answer/id #uuid "9100cb77-e0d2-59d4-94ab-8d24a15761ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716/selection/36bc1ac6bd10ae8956124d706163d9e0a8b0d6e3adae160f9abbb502675578e2" :answer/id #uuid "13f2aca9-b9d3-5196-867b-f272808766a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716/selection/f1a2c939fd528ad6a2de3616a7d9b33c165f688c389e744c0a4880ce7525bfea" :answer/id #uuid "6bbe01f4-528b-5d33-a90a-8d9ac2571b14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716/selection/bed174f4d5f6242f34b75832822278737ca4c6eb420c1069e233e49cc880c9fd" :answer/id #uuid "6b7b1e74-5e2b-553c-b055-29033c86538e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "067f38fd-0d37-5f3d-8fff-7a7d824c10f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159716/selection/f1a2c939fd528ad6a2de3616a7d9b33c165f688c389e744c0a4880ce7525bfea" :answer-field/choices ["q-159716/selection/269a36d49266519ed5dab217c7664817e5da284d03c67290a620939af15a036d" "q-159716/selection/13a2f7f94d95f46bf33f1c60a64505c798a5d8b7e91b2da1ffb8193348014d98" "q-159716/selection/36bc1ac6bd10ae8956124d706163d9e0a8b0d6e3adae160f9abbb502675578e2" "q-159716/selection/f1a2c939fd528ad6a2de3616a7d9b33c165f688c389e744c0a4880ce7525bfea" "q-159716/selection/bed174f4d5f6242f34b75832822278737ca4c6eb420c1069e233e49cc880c9fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159716" :question/id #uuid "068ab429-8193-5817-9f73-d6ab1bfc151f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159716" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))-{y}^{3}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =((4{x}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x))-{y}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159716/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "48c55673-9ed6-571b-8182-6f2df9653f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "2d7f292e-b10a-5a2d-b4a2-407df8c9ae72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d0b663cf-2c6b-5a52-b15c-a31438f539e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "7281c65f-e044-521a-a051-59324b55df69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "47f1c1d7-8a96-5058-ae6d-1bc793bffb0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03fef776-b21c-52e7-a3c9-ffea0fe6a3c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159709/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-159709/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-159709/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-159709/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-159709/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-159709/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159709" :question/id #uuid "c8a7e486-17de-592f-96c1-9311ddc05fcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-159709" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,2)} & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+0}{(2+0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159709/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2c11682d-984b-546b-bbca-cf94ac6506d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer/id #uuid "d0fe4f1e-f8f3-53dc-9103-6cee3e737266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b7c53be7-bdbd-5954-934b-b4a21d167629" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "23c7679d-ffe0-50d3-97db-0a1b7cbdb0b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "23e79b07-95ef-5d34-b6ed-e46b3a157e0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33ea1e05-94a1-505c-9621-87f953291990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159700/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-159700/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-159700/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" "q-159700/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-159700/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-159700/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159700" :question/id #uuid "bf13512e-3387-5291-88a0-4f86e5763eb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159700" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,\\pi /2)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159700/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159700"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159714/selection/251e683b07044b10bcc02a34481eaeb0cae7a2300489363820e3a7ac6ab2a057" :answer/id #uuid "2b6dc98b-68dd-5072-906d-8b9e815d01ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+xy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159714/selection/90b71ddb92f