h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot 2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=1-x{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159714/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159714"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713/selection/f2308547ba5be0db2ac44955ac1bed475ed6a0e61dd6044de147b7e59cc2bb51" :answer/id #uuid "85c9243f-2447-5aa8-b59a-d7f19a7d209a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713/selection/7beb3297af7ed369a3653be72bdc063f2b629de135c0700283f3a0062bfeef98" :answer/id #uuid "c41a924b-f2b1-5189-96b2-61bbc57a1a0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4y-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713/selection/dce6ecd27923fdd00ac4e611d401d65f9d9dd303a124dd1ba8b958cb9460f040" :answer/id #uuid "872afa34-b9d5-5d1f-b6a9-43b0753e333c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713/selection/1d8e4d4ca05809b4ff03e4ab5c8a87e8ac0dbc724f449ca6244d0db5e7d4cddb" :answer/id #uuid "a560833b-667b-5026-aa1b-a1b70d1b97c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713/selection/6480237784d6a35fde632a25d557390f228c753685f740cff4c4f9a721c0ce09" :answer/id #uuid "44ce801d-ad4f-58ec-a264-d436b4b0a9f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a68bbd05-c360-5161-b3fb-6b7b3f22bb66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159713/selection/f2308547ba5be0db2ac44955ac1bed475ed6a0e61dd6044de147b7e59cc2bb51" :answer-field/choices ["q-159713/selection/f2308547ba5be0db2ac44955ac1bed475ed6a0e61dd6044de147b7e59cc2bb51" "q-159713/selection/7beb3297af7ed369a3653be72bdc063f2b629de135c0700283f3a0062bfeef98" "q-159713/selection/dce6ecd27923fdd00ac4e611d401d65f9d9dd303a124dd1ba8b958cb9460f040" "q-159713/selection/1d8e4d4ca05809b4ff03e4ab5c8a87e8ac0dbc724f449ca6244d0db5e7d4cddb" "q-159713/selection/6480237784d6a35fde632a25d557390f228c753685f740cff4c4f9a721c0ce09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159713" :question/id #uuid "3b4241fc-d343-57db-b682-2b4f5e3dcd59" :question/math-academy-id "q-159713" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+y)\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+y})}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y))}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot 1)}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)-(3x+y)}{2\\sqrt{x+y}})}{x+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+5y}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=3x+5y.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159713/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159713"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723/selection/30d445c762f15dc71091f85d18a29a6dbef35e302e2c0b98b2c3e4c50cd59008" :answer/id #uuid "435df410-881b-58de-be34-afbbeb798f53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(2x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723/selection/bae54b25c51b837784b20763341effb55ad6296c9dd4e23bd682e29a9ec53ec7" :answer/id #uuid "80884e48-5e32-528e-998e-36d63b7ecacc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1-y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723/selection/5b8c669b5102c24f7cd077e51f87fe885aeaa5695159669f2a146699011ae088" :answer/id #uuid "e3733ea0-3278-579d-843c-17a435db6857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723/selection/4466a920c2aeb5ed2de2e54cda8fd3ecc021233b79e81e42c2b723f66f31bcdf" :answer/id #uuid "9e471127-6f76-5680-8bc2-db366149adb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-x{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723/selection/6db7a947cc9885c825cd7136ab6ed3e335a07e5b678fd0f0b9775ca45eba17cf" :answer/id #uuid "af57bbc0-a7d0-59e2-be79-1ed441456dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57441ed7-c123-5db0-9d04-b69822dfdf07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159723/selection/6db7a947cc9885c825cd7136ab6ed3e335a07e5b678fd0f0b9775ca45eba17cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-159723/selection/30d445c762f15dc71091f85d18a29a6dbef35e302e2c0b98b2c3e4c50cd59008" "q-159723/selection/bae54b25c51b837784b20763341effb55ad6296c9dd4e23bd682e29a9ec53ec7" "q-159723/selection/5b8c669b5102c24f7cd077e51f87fe885aeaa5695159669f2a146699011ae088" "q-159723/selection/4466a920c2aeb5ed2de2e54cda8fd3ecc021233b79e81e42c2b723f66f31bcdf" "q-159723/selection/6db7a947cc9885c825cd7136ab6ed3e335a07e5b678fd0f0b9775ca45eba17cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159723" :question/id #uuid "da6991b3-2060-51f5-9aca-09e2d4207eb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159723" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{y}^{2})}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{y}^{3}+2{x}^{2}y+2{y}^{3}}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy+2{x}^{2}y}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1+x)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=2xy(1+x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159723/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "15e881f3-118c-5fd3-a368-060757825e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer/id #uuid "8a7efc43-d3ce-53aa-b521-0885aded7a17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer/id #uuid "0d36358e-a40f-5cac-8f14-41e4aad501e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253/selection/71957986e85745e1f65d0d55b3bd3d256473176d34ec080119f8fcc44e63147e" :answer/id #uuid "bb7e62a2-9fc6-5910-b7b9-e15d9a9e860c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "54616207-a198-5962-9f81-131b777e1962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc6ea07-0fa3-5626-8a44-e35219654958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132253/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer-field/choices ["q-132253/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-132253/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" "q-132253/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" "q-132253/selection/71957986e85745e1f65d0d55b3bd3d256473176d34ec080119f8fcc44e63147e" "q-132253/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132253" :question/id #uuid "adb985bd-dcb3-5be8-a084-1d0889512850" :question/math-academy-id "q-132253" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(3,-1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}{({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{-1/2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (2x+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,-1,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(3,-1,-2)} & =\\frac{(3)(-1)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+4(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9+16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132253/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35710"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})-(0) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0,1)} & =2(1)^{2}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "d5b5115a-13ea-5805-9e42-7c6cde8ffeca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" :answer/id #uuid "3a62b068-ead1-5e8e-a97e-283c9c03776d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5b2b07b4-71a7-582e-8934-41bddaed16d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "bf5512d5-5fe2-558b-b20e-81f457504cd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer/id #uuid "7e1faa4d-aeb3-5a96-b91c-063b7e03c2f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cddf011a-baa1-5f8d-b037-db8d60d27eac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64907/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer-field/choices ["q-64907/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-64907/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" "q-64907/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-64907/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-64907/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64907" :question/id #uuid "d80f449c-f2b6-559b-a95b-ee208f9e4649" :question/math-academy-id "q-64907" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot 1-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}yz-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) & =yz-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz) \\\\  & =yz-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)\\cdot (z) \\\\  & =yz-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz) \\\\  & =z(y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,0,\\pi )} & =\\pi (0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi (0-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-64907/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812/selection/0565f1f20ec34d894ed97519d097802ce8cfc0aa64c42aeae8bbf469ecaccfd7" :answer/id #uuid "bc7cff8b-277b-53c5-8064-b15a1d07a4e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" :answer/id #uuid "4c88c154-868a-5769-9973-b30fdaa8e13f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812/selection/9089aefeda70249e88940c7b16f12f3ea57fd9d6f9c3fd57d03a8ecdf8270ed1" :answer/id #uuid "5e666248-9d96-5d9e-ab1c-74de23ef882f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812/selection/ff9edad0f999033589fa2d13aa4b8224ae05e2a716bc76c1210a8086cc5c1357" :answer/id #uuid "016c3b28-8204-5023-8aa6-a51db3e81287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812/selection/797c9896bf0d93eba6a0ebf00de4cd967649949dd38feb496afb1a629ab19ddf" :answer/id #uuid "afd0e988-1ddc-5407-b45c-5e8d4a7bddfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13d82bc1-c010-56e4-aa2a-21c043b106dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86812/selection/ff9edad0f999033589fa2d13aa4b8224ae05e2a716bc76c1210a8086cc5c1357" :answer-field/choices ["q-86812/selection/0565f1f20ec34d894ed97519d097802ce8cfc0aa64c42aeae8bbf469ecaccfd7" "q-86812/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" "q-86812/selection/9089aefeda70249e88940c7b16f12f3ea57fd9d6f9c3fd57d03a8ecdf8270ed1" "q-86812/selection/ff9edad0f999033589fa2d13aa4b8224ae05e2a716bc76c1210a8086cc5c1357" "q-86812/selection/797c9896bf0d93eba6a0ebf00de4cd967649949dd38feb496afb1a629ab19ddf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86812" :question/id #uuid "526dd47f-a660-5cfc-b389-d90165c8c680" :question/math-academy-id "q-86812" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}{e}^{xy}-{y}^{2}{e}^{yz},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}$ at the point $(0,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}{e}^{xy}-{y}^{2}{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}{e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{yz})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{yz}) & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot 2z-{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{yz}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot 2z-{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{yz}\\cdot y \\\\  & =2z{e}^{xy}-{y}^{3}{e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z}{|}_{(0,-1,1)} & =2(1){e}^{(0)(-1)}-(-1)^{3}{e}^{(-1)(1)} \\\\  & =2+{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721/selection/d916872fe653a70abbd2ce88439cbed339c0e8a0f1c56fc089e5fd7532575e9a" :answer/id #uuid "6cbc9ef1-ff62-5892-b411-81f4c7566911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721/selection/443e890fca3be46837aea015f677010b048ac449862130838cc92c05dace7ef9" :answer/id #uuid "c0541915-547b-5738-9c8b-c4e026b5a12f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z-(z+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721/selection/fc4114a8152e27776978d37f015a955d8d9ef2647eaa4b2299fa80ed55b11f08" :answer/id #uuid "ab8c69f2-94af-542c-873a-e94551e3f14e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721/selection/b35beb0ec42528763ce302630db8d9a1c778ae75d350a48be968a0229f1a8d02" :answer/id #uuid "feeadf0d-b352-541f-8bde-48ef85847b69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721/selection/2bda880b79a139a1ef952dc638b91307f9f478db062c6408b1c8b342036409c3" :answer/id #uuid "a7ce38b5-5a75-546e-8286-4537895fb589" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4168855-2873-5868-b164-a249883a4198" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35721/selection/2bda880b79a139a1ef952dc638b91307f9f478db062c6408b1c8b342036409c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-35721/selection/d916872fe653a70abbd2ce88439cbed339c0e8a0f1c56fc089e5fd7532575e9a" "q-35721/selection/443e890fca3be46837aea015f677010b048ac449862130838cc92c05dace7ef9" "q-35721/selection/fc4114a8152e27776978d37f015a955d8d9ef2647eaa4b2299fa80ed55b11f08" "q-35721/selection/b35beb0ec42528763ce302630db8d9a1c778ae75d350a48be968a0229f1a8d02" "q-35721/selection/2bda880b79a139a1ef952dc638b91307f9f478db062c6408b1c8b342036409c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35721" :question/id #uuid "191a6c22-e38e-5a60-a84b-fb853e195152" :question/math-academy-id "q-35721" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{z}(x,y,z)$ for $g(x,y,z)=(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(z+y) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35721/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35721"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-11048"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) =\\ln(y-x^2),$ evaluate $f_x(1,9).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-{x}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot 0-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,9)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,9) & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{9-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-11028"] :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ for $f(x,y) =x^2y\\ln{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & =y\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =y\\cdot ((2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})) \\\\  & =y(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x) \\\\  & =xy(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-11112"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{4x-y}{x+y^2},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4x-y}{x+{y}^{2}}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x-y)\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2})}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot 1}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x+4{y}^{2}-4x+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(2,-1)} & =\\frac{4(-1)^{2}+(-1)}{{(2+{(-1)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-11027"] :question/problem "For the function  $g(x,y,z) = 2 (x + 1)e^z+ yz,$  evaluate  $\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial z}$ at $(1,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x+1){e}^{z}+yz) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x+1){e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & =2(x+1)\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{z}+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z}{|}_{(1,1,1)} & =2(1+1){e}^{1}+1 \\\\  & =4e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
